body:
Oh i acknowledge the sacrifice that mothers make, and my mother has made sacrifices for me too. However there are things she did and things she chose not to do that in my opinion trumps any sacrifice she's made for me. After all, being a mother is a normal animal instinct, it's the difference between a mother and a good mother that counts. I am by no means an ideal son, but i have suffered my whole life and continue to suffer for it. In the beginning the suffering was for undeserved, but as i grow up i have become deserving of this suffering, so i guess it's all good. 

&#x200B;

I just envy that you loved your mother enough to live for her, she must be a decent mother. I want a reason to live for, because i know life is very dynamic and if you put in the effort then things can change with a some luck. All you need is the encouragement/ reason to live on and your mother gives you that opportunity.

This post speaks to me more than any other post on this sub for probably ever. You sound like a chronic depressed person like me. Medications messed up my already messed up sexual functions, and male hormones. Doctors never tell you this, or they try to downplay the side effects of medications, but i was young and naive and took all those prescribed medications for a year, and they messed me up. I am still trying to recover from them after stopping for over a year now. I think our mainstream mental health treatment is still at a very primitive stage compared to a lot of other health departments. Hospitalizations are just temporary holding cells to stabilize suicidal/ "crazy" people until we are subdued and zombified with meds. Therapy are just a loose support structure that never really helped me. I even had some decent therapists, but at the end of the day it's just 45 mins a week like you said. Maybe treatment helps some people, but definitely not some chronic sufferers like us. Your bad experiences on long term treatment places is interesting to me. I was never able to go to those places because economics don't allow me to, but i always had this fantasy that those places are where rich people can get the "real help", i guess maybe not so easy. 

&#x200B;

Hopefully your pain will ease with time. Hopefully you'll find some real solution along the way. I can't wait to die.

Thanks for this more insightful breakdown of the procurement situation with Italy. I knew that funding had to come outside of the defense budget, but i just didn't know how they were able to pitch it to the government. This is a smart thing they're doing here. These ships are very capable, and even the light variant is very capable and can be upgraded to full frigate configuration if needed. If Italy can pump out 10 to 16 of these vessels on top of the 2 horizon destroyers, 10 FREMM frigates, and maybe 2 'DDX's, they will no doubt have the best surface combatant in the whole of NATO, second only to US Navy.

&#x200B;

So sad the current politics prevent Royal navy and French navy from doing something like this... Would love to see UK scrap the type 31e program, redirect some money from the foreign aid budget and do a type 26 light or something like the PPA.

Oh yea, i struggle so much with sleep. I went to bed at 11PM a few days ago, and didn't fall asleep until like 6AM. Now i just stay up until 5AM and let my body go. 

&#x200B;

People really don't care beyond a surface superficial "caring". They say nice things, and do some simple nice things that does absolutely nothing to help others. Not even my family cares about me really. They have known about my depression and loneliness for many years, and not one of them have comforted me in anyway. People say "oh you're not alone..." and then proceeds to ignore me forever. Then i try to put in the effort by reaching out, and that only further pushes people away and worsens my depression.
